    context: "Revelation 12 draws on Genesis 3:15 and the birth of the Messiah. The dragon is identified as the ancient serpent, the devil. The woman is variously seen as Israel, Mary, the church or all God's people. The beasts of chapter 13 draw from Daniel 7 and probably represented Rome and its imperial cult to first readers, while also representing recurring patterns of idolatrous power. The mark contrasts with the seal of God. Chapter 14 offers consolation and warning, with the Lamb and his followers, the eternal gospel, the fall of Babylon and the harvest of the earth.",
